\\ 1 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nDetermine whether $A=PD{P}^{-1}$ for some invertible matrix $P$ and a diagonal matrix $D,$ where $P$ and $D$ are both real. In the affirmative case, find a possible diagonal matrix $D.$" 13194139535919 true] [17592186374374 1113 #uuid "2b91b641-543b-5493-9c2b-612e261c9581" 13194139535919 true] [17592186374374 1145 "First, we need to determine whether $D$ is diagonalizable over $R.$\n\nWe start by computing the eigenvalues of $A.$ To do that, we solve the characteristic equation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}1-\\lambda  & 0 & -5 \\\\ 1 & 7-\\lambda  & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -1-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (7-\\lambda )|\\begin{aligned}1-\\lambda  & -5 \\\\ 1 & -1-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (7-\\lambda )((1-\\lambda )(-1-\\lambda )+5) & =0 \\\\ (7-\\lambda )({\\lambda }^{2}+4) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the quadratic polynomial $\\,{\\lambda }^{2}+4\\,$ we have that the discriminant $D<0.$ So, it doesn't have real roots. \n\nTherefore, $A$ is not diagonalizable over $R.$" 13194139535919 true] [17592186374375 1000 #edb/ref 17592186374376 13194139535919 true] [17592186374375 1000 #edb/ref 17592186374377 13194139535919 true] [17592186374375 1000 #edb/ref 17592186374378 13194139535919 true] [17592186374375 1000 #edb/ref 17592186374379 13194139535919 true] [17592186374375 1000 #edb/ref 17592186374380 13194139535919 true] [17592186374375 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535919 true] [17592186374375 1041 "selection" 13194139535919 true] [17592186374375 1104 #edb/ref 17592186374380 13194139535919 true] [17592186374375 1110 #uuid "71fc6fb1-5b6f-5cd9-9b5b-ec39f8051077" 13194139535919 true] [17592186374376 1034 "D=[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]" 13194139535919 true] [17592186374376 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535919 true] [17592186374376 1111 #uuid "51b4f2f3-963f-5fe5-9f5b-e00ec999df2c" 13194139535919 true] [17592186374377 1034